        /// <summary>
        /// Replaces the credential of a tunnel account and ends every environment enabled with it, shares and all, so a credential handed out before — to a member who has left, or to anyone who read it — opens nothing from now on. Replaces the credential of a tunnel account and ends every environment enabled with it, shares and all, so a credential handed out before — to a member who has left, or to anyone who read it — opens nothing from now on. The account is kept: enable hands its holder the new credential.  In a customer&#39;s org the account is the org&#39;s, which its members share, and an admin of the org or a SuperAdmin rotates it. In a held org each person&#39;s account is their own, and they rotate it — every account they hold, the one an API key of theirs was handed before included, so none stays live. An admin of the org or a SuperAdmin then rotates the org&#39;s own account, which no call there hands out, whether or not they hold an account of their own; when that one cannot be rotated, &#x60;pending&#x60; says so and their own are rotated still.  An account never provisioned has nothing to rotate and counts 0. 503 when the deployment has no share controller configured; 502 when that controller is unreachable, or holds the caller&#39;s account under a credential this deployment does not derive — out of a rotation&#39;s reach, so it is refused rather than reported done.
